<title>FRANCE: U.S. top origin for Paris '96 air imports.</title>
<headline>U.S. top origin for Paris '96 air imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal</p>
<p>country of origin for import traffic handled at the Paris</p>
<p>airports in 1996, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris</p>
<p>(ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The principal countries of origin for ADP import in 1996, with percentage change on 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	   150,524    up    3.6pct</p>
<p> 2  India			28,583    up   20.4</p>
<p> 3  Japan			20,671    down  5.1</p>
<p> 4  Hong Kong		  20,360    down  2.6</p>
<p> 5  Canada		     20,220    down  1.3</p>
<p> 6  United Kingdom	   18,331    up    3.1</p>
<p> 7  Germany		    15,538    up   31.1</p>
<p> 8  Italy			12,677    up    4.1</p>
<p> 9  Thailand		   11,727    down 11.0</p>
<p> 10 Kenya			10,385    down  5.6</p>
<p> 11 French West Indies	7,866    down  3.7</p>
<p> 12 Senegal		     7,506    up   42.1</p>
<p> 13 United Arab Emirates    7,054    down  6.9</p>
<p> 14 Morocco		     6,694    down 10.6</p>
<p> 15 Argentina		   6,422    up   18.8</p>
<p> 16 South Africa		6,215    up   11.7</p>
<p> 17 China			 5,842    up    6.3</p>
<p> 18 Singapore		   5,820    up    7.1</p>
<p> 19 Brazil			5,819    down 26.0</p>
<p> 20 Switzerland		 5,312    up    9.1</p>
<p> Total top 20 origins     373,566</p>
<p> Total all origins	  523,817    up    2.6</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
